{"id":"chatcmpl-3866f6e4-16f5-4741-b8c1-5446ca20d4a2","object":"chat.completion","created":1795244552,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a multi-tool consensus strategy for medical image interpretation: query multiple independent vision-language models with the same targeted question, then use grounded localization to spatially verify the finding before committing to an answer. The key insight is that laterality (left vs. right) is a common failure mode, so spatial grounding coordinates serve as an objective tiebreaker. Cross-validation across heterogeneous tools reduces single-model hallucination risk.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question hinges on spatial laterality (left/right), always pair semantic model queries with a grounded localization tool that returns coordinates, and map coordinates to patient-side anatomy before answering.\",\n    \"Query at least two independent vision-language models with the same targeted question and treat agreement as confidence; disagreement triggers deeper spatial verification.\",\n    \"Decompose the question into a presence check plus a location check (e.g., 'is X present?' then 'which side?') rather than asking the compound question once.\",\n    \"Use a phrase-grounding tool on the specific finding name to obtain objective evidence, and let coordinate ranges (not model prose) arbitrate the final answer.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Ask a targeted presence+location question to multiple VLMs, then confirm with a grounding/localization tool; use coordinates to resolve laterality disputes.\",\n    \"Visual attribute verification\": \"Separate 'does it exist' from 'where/what attribute' into distinct queries; use spatial or measurable evidence as the tiebreaker over free-text model claims.\",\n    \"Multi-tool consensus reasoning\": \"Run parallel independent tools on the same sub-question, require agreement for high confidence, and escalate to a more objective tool when they conflict.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the finding's coordinates map to the correct patient side (radiological convention: image-left = patient-right) before selecting a laterality answer.\",\n    \"Verify that at least two independent tools agree on presence and side; if not, trust the grounded localization evidence over model prose.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":512,"total_tokens":938,"completion_tokens":426,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":512},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":426}}}